messages:
maria_p: Quick thread to align on a 'role compatibility' migration playbook for the chat endpoint. Customers keep sending a mix of `prompt` strings and `messages` arrays with all kinds of role names (bot, assistant, system, instruction, customer). We need a minimal, safe path to accept both shapes and provide predictable semantics + observability. Thoughts? :clipboard:
aj: agree we need predictable semantics. Proposal: canonical server model is messages[] with roles {system, user, assistant}. Server accepts payloads with either `prompt` or `messages`. If `prompt` present -> convert to an initial `system` message by default. Important: allow opt-out via header if customer intentionally used different semantics.
sam_g: ML/behavior risk: some models treat the first message as higher weight (system) vs prefix. Converting `prompt` -> `system` could change outputs for a subset of models. We should run a regression that compares: prompt-as-system vs prompt-as-merged-user across top N models and thresholds for QA.
nisha_ml: agree. Suggest we ship with two modes behind FF: `prompt_as_system` (default) and `prompt_as_user` (opt-in for legacy parity). Record which mode used in traces and eval logs. Also record token delta impact and top-k divergence metric.
diego: ops requests: we must expose a compatibility header for routing/metrics: `X-RW-Input-Shape: prompt|messages|mixed`. Also include `X-RW-Role-Map-Version` so we can roll role-mapping changes without losing telemetry.
emma_pm: migration playbook (high level): 1) server adapter accepts both shapes; 2) emit compat header + annotation in audit logs; 3) run A/B canary where 5% of traffic uses normalized messages; 4) collect divergence metrics and error rates for two weeks; 5) SDKs provide a helper lib to convert prompt->messages to encourage client migration.
oliver_d: eval suggestions: assemble 200 representative customer prompts (from opt-in telemetry) and run delta tests: token usage, returned function-calls, hallucination rate, and safety classifier score. Set pass/fail thresholds (e.g., hallucination delta < 2%, function-call retention > 99%).
author: maria_p: concrete role mapping rules I propose shipping immediately: - case-insensitive mapping: 'assistant', 'bot', 'systembot' -> assistant; 'system', 'instructions', 'context' -> system; anything else -> user. Include telemetry for unmapped tokens.
aj: add fallback rule: if the first message after normalization is extremely long (>2k tokens), don't auto-promote prompt to system; instead keep as user and flag for review. This avoids accidentally moving large user content into system slot.
sam_g: example canonicalization pseudocode we can ship in server: ```
// payload: { prompt?: string, messages?: [{role, content}] }
messages = []
if (payload.prompt) {
  // respect feature flag to choose mapping target
  targetRole = FF.enabled('prompt_as_system') ? 'system' : 'user'
  messages.push({role: targetRole, content: payload.prompt, _meta: {origin: 'prompt'}})
}
if (payload.messages) {
  payload.messages.forEach(m => {
    normalized = {role: roleMap[m.role.toLowerCase()] || 'user', content: m.content, _meta: {orig_role: m.role}}
    messages.push(normalized)
  })
}
// produce final canonical_messages array and persisted trace
```
diego: caching note: to keep prefix-KV and response cache efficiency we should compute a canonical hash over canonical_messages where whitespace normalized and role order normalized. This will let equivalent inputs map to the same cache key. We'll need a migration window to backfill frequently-hit keys.
emma_pm: launch criteria proposal (must-have to GA): - Canonical adapter behind FF and enabled for canary - Compatibility header + role map version emitted - SDK helper libraries published (js/python) with examples - Regression evals pass thresholds on top 3 models - No >10% increase in p95 latency for normalization path - Audit logs persist original payload + normalized messages with origin flags - Runbook for rollback and customer support prepared
chloe_sre (infra-bot placeholder): scheduled canary deployment for region us-west-2 next Tue; will enable FF for 5% traffic and monitor errors/latency. Tagging resources: FF-5087.
maria_p: follow-up items + owners: - RFC doc + test matrix: me (maria_p) - Server impl + roleMap table: aj + sam_g - SDK helpers + migration guide: aj + docs - Regression evals + dataset curation: oliver_d + nisha_ml - Caching/hash spec + infra changes: diego - Runbook + support playbook: emma_pm - Telemetry dashboards: diego + oliver_d
aj: can we also add a small telemetry counter for "role-remap events" so PM/eng can see the distribution of incoming unknown roles? That helps prioritize aliases.
maria_p: good call — add to dashboard requirements. I'll drop a short RFC with the roleMap table proposal and sample migration snippets. Thanks all :raised_hands:
